{"name":"East Aurora","hex":"#878b46","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"East Aurora","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A village in the town of Aurora, Erie County, New York, United States."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/East_Aurora"}],"entries":[{"title":"East Aurora, New York","blocks":[{"text":"East Aurora is a village in Erie County, New York, United States, southeast of Buffalo. It lies in the eastern half of the town of Aurora. The village population was 5,998 per the 2020 census. It is part of the Buffalo–Niagara Falls metropolitan area. In 2015, East Aurora was rated the third-best town to raise a family in New York State by Niche. According to the National Council of Home Safety and Security, it is also among the safest places to live in New York State. The village is included on the List of Tree Cities USA."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Aurora_Theatre_from_Main_Street.jpg/330px-Aurora_Theatre_from_Main_Street.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East_Aurora%2C_New_York","wikidata":"Q1019210"},{"title":"East","blocks":[{"text":"East is one of the four cardinal directions or points of the compass. It is the opposite direction from west and is the direction from which the Sun rises on the Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Compass_Rose_English_East.svg/330px-Compass_Rose_English_East.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/East","wikidata":"Q684"},{"title":"Aurora","blocks":[{"text":"An aurora is a natural light display in Earth's upper atmosphere caused by charged particles from the Sun colliding with atoms in the atmosphere. These collisions excite oxygen and nitrogen, which then emit light of different colours such as green, red, and purple. When observed in high-latitude regions they are called polar lights and aurora polaris. In the Arctic they are called the northern lights or aurora borealis; in the Antarctic, the term southern lights or aurora australis is used. Auroras display dynamic patterns of radiant light that appear as curtains, rays, spirals or dynamic flickers covering the entire sky."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Aurora_borealis_over_Eielson_Air_Force_Base%2C_Alaska.jpg/330px-Aurora_borealis_over_Eielson_Air_Force_Base%2C_Alaska.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aurora","wikidata":"Q40609"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/cc/EastAuroraNYseal.png/120px-EastAuroraNYseal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/cc/EastAuroraNYseal.png/250px-EastAuroraNYseal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/cc/EastAuroraNYseal.png/120px-EastAuroraNYseal.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEastAuroraNYseal.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Millard_Fillmore_Presidential_Site%2C_East_Aurora_NY_2017.jpg/500px-Millard_Fillmore_Presidential_Site%2C_East_Aurora_NY_2017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Millard_Fillmore_Presidential_Site%2C_East_Aurora_NY_2017.jpg/1280px-Millard_Fillmore_Presidential_Site%2C_East_Aurora_NY_2017.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Millard_Fillmore_Presidential_Site%2C_East_Aurora_NY_2017.jpg/500px-Millard_Fillmore_Presidential_Site%2C_East_Aurora_N